== Production ==
''Hulk and the Agents of S.M.A.S.H.'' was unveiled at the 2011 San Diego Comic Con.<ref name="Marvel.com">{{Cite web |last=Collura |first=Scott |date=2011-07-23 |title=Comic-Con: Hulk Smashes New Team Cartoon |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2011/07/23/comic-con-hulk-smashes-new-team-cartoon |access-date= |website=[[IGN]] |language=en}}</ref> Pre-production was outsourced to New Zealand-based company Karactaz Animation.<ref name="stuff">{{cite news|url=http://www.stuff.co.nz/business/small-business/8606735/Animation-company-does-Hulking-job|title=Animation company does Hulking job|last1=McNicol|first1=Hamish|date=April 29, 2013|access-date=July 27, 2014|publisher=stuff.co.nz}}</ref> [[Film Roman]] was contracted to produce.<ref name="am">{{cite news|url=http://www.animationmagazine.net/tv/dushku-is-she-hulk-in-new-disney-xd-show/|title=Dushku is She-Hulk in New Disney XD Show|last1=Milligan|first1=Mercedes|date=April 18, 2012|work=Animation Magazine|access-date=October 26, 2015}}</ref> Before it aired, writers [[Paul Dini]] and [[Henry Gilroy]] were confirmed to be writing for the series.<ref name="Cast 2" /> Supervising producer Cort Lane described the series as, "a great story about a great group of characters who have a really interesting family-style dynamic. It's very funny, with just the most amazing voice cast."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ching |first=Albert |date=January 21, 2013 |title=Things Get Personal for ULTIMATE SPIDER-MAN in Season 2 |url=http://www.newsarama.com/tv/ultimate-spider-man-cort-lane.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130124204012/http://www.newsarama.com/tv/ultimate-spider-man-cort-lane.html |archive-date=January 24, 2013}}</ref> On July 26, 2014, the series was renewed for a second season.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://variety.com/2014/tv/news/disney-xd-renews-avengers-hulk-marvel-cartoons-1201269592/|title=Disney XD Renews Marvel's 'Avengers Assemble,' 'Hulk and the Agents of S.M.A.S.H.'|last1=Khatchatourian|first1=Maane|date=July 26, 2014|work=Variety|access-date=July 28, 2014}}</ref>

On July 12, 2015, Marvel Animation vice president [[Stephen Wacker]] confirmed that the series had ended after the second season.<ref name="How to fail upwards!"/>

== Broadcast ==
The series premiered on [[Teletoon]] in Canada on January 10, 2014,<ref>{{cite web |title=TELETOON Canada Inc. - TELETOON Canada's Comedy-Filled Lineup Delivers Warm Laughter this Winter |url=http://www.newswire.ca/en/story/1269457/teletoon-canada-s-comedy-filled-lineup-delivers-warm-laughter-this-winter |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140519223035/https://www.newswire.ca/en/story/1269457/teletoon-canada-s-comedy-filled-lineup-delivers-warm-laughter-this-winter/ |archive-date=May 19, 2014 |access-date=March 16, 2015 |work=newswire.ca}}</ref> and on April 13, 2014 on [[CITV]] in the United Kingdom.<ref>{{cite web |last=Higgins |first=D |date=April 8, 2014 |title=New this week on Foxtel: Game of Thrones, Veep, Silicon Valley and two new Disney channels |url=http://community.foxtel.com.au/t5/Foxtel-Blog/New-this-week-on-Foxtel-Game-of-Thrones-Veep-Silicon-Valley-and/ba-p/12875 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140414000812/http://community.foxtel.com.au/t5/Foxtel-Blog/New-this-week-on-Foxtel-Game-of-Thrones-Veep-Silicon-Valley-and/ba-p/12875 |archive-date=April 14, 2014 |access-date=March 16, 2015 |work=Foxtel |publisher=}}</ref>

== Reception ==
Jesse Schedeen of [[IGN]] gave the show's premiere a "Mediocre" score of 5.8 out of 10, panning the show's reliance on humor, which came at the expense of dramatic weight. Schedeen surmised that the series was targeted primarily at young boys and summarized it as "a disappointing new addition to Disney XD's growing Marvel lineup".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=2013-08-12 |title=''Hulk and the Agents of S.M.A.S.H.'': "Doorway to Destruction" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2013/08/12/hulk-and-the-agents-of-smash-doorway-to-destruction-review |access-date= |website=IGN |language=en}}</ref>

